# Shared agent policy

Follow [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) at the repo root for Next.js, TypeScript, SOLID, theme, docs, and git commits.

Modular twins: [`.agents/rules/`](../../.agents/rules/) — `agents-policy.md`, `typescript-standards.md`, `solid-principles.md`, `theme.md`, `git-commits.md`.

Match existing patterns under `app/` as the console grows; planned Go control plane lives under `cmd/` / `internal/` per `docs/architecture.md`.

Non-negotiables:

- Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before changing framework behavior
- No secrets in git; no inventing infra/CDK/deploy unless asked
- Missing OIDC/required env → fail loud (no silent auth fallback UI)
- Product UI → `docs/theme.md`
- Commits only when the user asks → `git-commits.mdc`

TypeScript & SOLID details: `.agents/rules/typescript-standards.md`, `.agents/rules/solid-principles.md`.
